                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love foxes. \n\nI love strawberries.\n\nThis game has plenty of both! \n\nBut it's... not really a game. It's more of a proof of concept of a game. It's a very nice looking concept of a game, with a nicely rendered geometric fox that is nicely animated, and that fox navigates a simple and stylish world. But the actual game itself is pretty low on difficulty. Find a star. Find a flower. Find a cake. Find a fox. That's about it. Oh, and you have to do all of these not-at-all-difficult tasks while avoiding some sort of rat-bunny-beaver things that are bouncing around and explode when you get too close to them.  Not that there are any apparent consequences for getting bunny bombed. You just shake it off and move along.\n\nFor full price (especially the price of $59.99 as of this writing) it's not worth it AT ALL. But if during a Steam sale it can be had for a buck or so? It's maaaaybe worth supporting a lone developer.\n\n(Oh, and don't let the time-played of 4.7 hours fool you. I must have opened it and then went to a movie or something because the entire game can be finished in 30-40 minutes)",
